// Output layout, split out of niri.config.kdl because TWO niri
// instances need it: the session (which includes this file — niri
// resolves relative includes against ~/.config/niri/, where both
// files are linked) and the DMS greeter, whose launcher appends
// `include "/etc/greetd/niri_overrides.kdl"` to its own generated
// config when that file exists — modules/nixos/greeter.nix points
// it at a store copy of this one. Without that, the greeter runs
// every monitor untransformed at scale 1: sideways on the vertical
// monitor, tiny on the 4K. (The greeter copy updates on rebuild, not
// on save — only the session hot-reloads.)
//
// Multi-machine convention: outputs are keyed by connector name, and a
// block for a connector the machine doesn't have is inert — this ONE
// file serves every host; add blocks, never fork it. eDP-1 exists only
// on the laptop. On a machine with other monitors, run `niri msg
// outputs` for their connector names and add a block per monitor here
// (position/mode/scale — the commented template in niri.config.kdl
// shows the fields); until then they auto-place in connector order.
//
// 1.0 slightly small, DMS's next preset 1.25 way too big — niri takes
// arbitrary fractional scales, and wayland-native apps stay crisp via
// the fractional-scale protocol (xwayland apps may soften slightly)
output "eDP-1" {
    scale 1.1
}

// hero: two monitors, left to right — the 1440p VERTICAL on HDMI-A-1,
// the 4K on DP-3. Connector-keyed, so these blocks
// are inert on the laptop (which has only eDP-1). Modes are each
// panel's maximum — the 1440p's preferred mode is a lazy 60 Hz, so
// the 320 Hz mode must be pinned or that is what you get. The 4K is
// centred against the portrait's 2048 logical height
// ((2048-1234)/2 = 407) so the cursor crosses at a steady height.
//
// The desk works as: the portrait holds static/reading things, the 4K
// is the scrollable workspace. Verify connector names with `niri msg
// outputs` after any cable change — the layout follows the PORT, not
// the panel.
//
// transform "270" is the rotation source (if text ever renders
// upside down, the fix is "90" here). Do NOT add a panel_orientation
// kernel param alongside it: niri COMPOSES the two.
//
// Portrait logical size at scale 1.25: 1440/1.25 = 1152 exactly, so
// the 4K's x=1152 has no fractional-overlap trap — keep the division
// exact if the scale ever changes.
output "HDMI-A-1" {
    mode "2560x1440@320.001"
    transform "270"
    scale 1.25
    position x=0 y=0
}

output "DP-3" {
    mode "3840x2160@240.000"
    scale 1.75
    position x=1152 y=407
}
